<div class="container">

<header>
  <h1>Why Is the Sky Blue?
    <span class="zh">天空为什么是蓝色的？</span>
  </h1>
</header>

<!-- ===== Toddler ===== -->
<div class="section">
  <div class="section-title">🧒 For a 3-Year-Old &nbsp;|&nbsp; 给3岁小朋友</div>
  <div class="cols">
    <div class="col">
      <h3>English</h3>
      <p>You know how when you shine a flashlight through a rainbow prism, you see all the colors spread out? Sunlight works the same way — it's made of lots of colors mixed together.</p>
      <p>When sunlight hits the air around us, the tiny bits of air bump the light around. The blue parts of the light get bumped around the most, so they bounce all over the sky in every direction. That's why when you look up, blue is the color that comes back to your eyes from all around!</p>
      <p>The red and orange colors don't bounce around as much, so they mostly keep going. That's also why sunsets look orange and red — you're seeing the light that managed to travel straight to you without bouncing off the blue stuff.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="col">
      <h3>中文</h3>
      <p>你知道吗，当你把手电筒的光照到彩虹三棱镜上时，会看到所有颜色散开吗？阳光也是这样的——它是由很多颜色混合在一起的。</p>
      <p>当阳光照到周围的空气上时，空气中的微小颗粒会把光四处弹开。蓝色的光被弹开得最厉害，所以在天空中向四面八方弹来弹去。这就是为什么你抬头看天空时，从各个方向映入你眼中的都是蓝色！</p>
      <p>红色和橙色的光弹得没那么多，所以它们大部分继续往前走了。这也是为什么日落时天空看起来是橙色和红色的——你看到的是那些成功直直地传到你眼前、没有和蓝色光一起弹走的光。</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- ===== High School ===== -->
<div class="section">
  <div class="section-title">🎓 For a High School Student &nbsp;|&nbsp; 给高中生</div>
  <div class="cols">
    <div class="col">
      <h3>English</h3>
      <p>The sky is blue because of a process called <strong>Rayleigh scattering</strong>.</p>
      <p>Sunlight looks white, but it's actually a mix of all visible wavelengths (roughly 380–700 nm). As sunlight enters Earth's atmosphere, it collides with gas molecules (mostly N₂ and O₂). These molecules are much smaller than the wavelength of visible light, and they scatter shorter wavelengths far more efficiently than longer ones.</p>
      <p>The key result from electromagnetic theory is that the scattering cross-section scales as:</p>
      <div class="formula">σ ∝ 1/λ⁴</div>
      <p>This means blue light (~450 nm) is scattered roughly <strong>(700/450)⁴ ≈ 10× more</strong> than red light (~700 nm). The scattered blue light is redirected in all directions, so no matter where you look in the sky, some of that scattered blue reaches your eyes.</p>
      <p>This also explains sunsets: when the Sun is low on the horizon, sunlight passes through a much longer path of atmosphere. By the time it reaches you, most of the blue has been scattered away, leaving the redder wavelengths dominant.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="col">
      <h3>中文</h3>
      <p>天空是蓝色的，原因在于一种叫做<strong>瑞利散射</strong>的过程。</p>
      <p>阳光看起来是白色的，但实际上它包含了所有可见光波长（大约380–700纳米）的混合。当阳光进入地球大气层时，会与气体分子（主要是N₂和O₂）发生碰撞。这些分子比可见光的波长小得多，它们对较短波长的散射效率远高于较长波长的。</p>
      <p>电磁理论的关键结论是，散射截面与波长的关系为：</p>
      <div class="formula">σ ∝ 1/λ⁴</div>
      <p>这意味着蓝光（约450纳米）被散射的程度大约是红光（约700纳米）的 <strong>(700/450)⁴ ≈ 10倍</strong>。被散射的蓝光被重新定向到各个方向，所以无论你看天空的哪个位置，总有一些散射蓝光到达你的眼睛。</p>
      <p>这也解释了日落现象：当太阳靠近地平线时，阳光穿过大气层的路径要长得多。等光线到达你时，大部分蓝光已经被散射走了，剩下的以红波长为主。</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- ===== Physics PhD ===== -->
<div class="section">
  <div class="section-title">🔬 For a Physics PhD &nbsp;|&nbsp; 给物理学博士</div>
  <div class="cols">
    <div class="col">
      <h3>English</h3>
      <p>The blue color of the sky is a consequence of <strong>elastic scattering of electromagnetic radiation by molecular-scale inhomogeneities in a dielectric medium</strong>, specifically described by <strong>Rayleigh's theory</strong> in the limit where the scattering particle radius <em>a</em> ≪ <em>λ</em> (the Rayleigh regime, |<em>mak</em>| ≪ 1).</p>

      <p><strong>The Microscopic Origin</strong></p>
      <p>The relevant polarization tensor for a sphere of dielectric constant ε in a uniform incident field E₀ is:</p>
      <div class="formula">α = 4πε₀a³ · (ε−1)/(ε+2)</div>
      <p>The induced dipole <strong>p</strong> = α<strong>E₀</strong> then reradiates. The differential scattering cross-section in the Rayleigh limit is:</p>
      <div class="formula">dσ/dΩ = (2π/λ)⁴ a⁶ |(ε−1)/(ε+2)|² (1 − |n̂·ŝ|²)</div>
      <p>giving a total cross-section:</p>
      <div class="formula">σ = (8π/3)(2πa/λ)⁴ a² |(ε−1)/(ε+2)|²</div>
      <p>The <strong>λ⁻⁴ dependence</strong> arises from: induced dipole moment ∝ a³, far-field amplitude ∝ a³/λ², cross-section ∝ a⁶/λ⁴.</p>

      <p><strong>Why Blue Specifically</strong></p>
      <p>For N₂ and O₂ at STP, number density ≈ 2.5×10²⁵ m⁻³. Mean free path ~ tens of meters, so the atmosphere is a dilute collection of independent scatterers (<em>ka</em> ≪ 1). Optical depth for blue light over a zenith path: τ ≈ 0.1–0.3 (single-scattering albedo of a few percent).</p>
      <p>Why <em>blue</em> rather than <em>violet</em>:</p>
      <ol>
        <li><strong>Solar spectrum</strong>: Planck spectrum (~5800 K) has lower photon flux in violet/UV.</li>
        <li><strong>Spectral sensitivity</strong>: Eye response peaks at 507/555 nm; lens absorbs short-wavelength light (purkinje effect reversal).</li>
      </ol>

      <p><strong>Beyond Rayleigh</strong></p>
      <p>At UV wavelengths, <em>ka</em> → 1, entering the <strong>Mie</strong> regime (full Mie series / spherical Bessel functions). For aerosols (a ~ 0.1–10 μm), Mie scattering is nearly wavelength-independent over visible range → polluted/hazy skies appear white/gray.</p>
      <p>Angular dependence &amp; polarization (~40% linearly polarized at 90° from Sun) follow from the vector dipole radiation pattern — consistent with a simple polarizing filter.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="col">
      <h3>中文</h3>
      <p>天空的蓝色是<strong>介电介质中分子尺度不均匀区域对电磁辐射的弹性散射</strong>的结果，具体由<strong>瑞利理论</strong>描述，适用于散射粒子半径 <em>a</em> ≪ <em>λ</em> 的极限（瑞利区，|<em>mak</em>| ≪ 1）。</p>

      <p><strong>微观起源</strong></p>
      <p>对于介电常数为 ε 的球体处于均匀入射场 E₀ 中，相关的极化张量为：</p>
      <div class="formula">α = 4πε₀a³ · (ε−1)/(ε+2)</div>
      <p>感应偶极矩 <strong>p</strong> = α<strong>E₀</strong> 随后重新辐射。瑞利极限下的微分散射截面为：</p>
      <div class="formula">dσ/dΩ = (2π/λ)⁴ a⁶ |(ε−1)/(ε+2)|² (1 − |n̂·ŝ|²)</div>
      <p>总截面为：</p>
      <div class="formula">σ = (8π/3)(2πa/λ)⁴ a² |(ε−1)/(ε+2)|²</div>
      <p><strong>λ⁻⁴ 依赖关系</strong>源于：感应偶极矩 ∝ a³，远场振幅 ∝ a³/λ²，截面 ∝ a⁶/λ⁴。</p>

      <p><strong>为什么偏偏是蓝色</strong></p>
      <p>对于标准状况下的 N₂ 和 O₂，数密度约为 2.5×10²⁵ m⁻³。散射事件之间的平均自由程约为数十米量级，大气可视为稀薄的独立散射体集合（<em>ka</em> ≪ 1）。蓝光沿天顶方向的光学厚度 τ ≈ 0.1–0.3（单次散射反照率约百分之几）。</p>
      <p>颜色是<em>蓝色</em>而非<em>紫色</em>有两个原因：</p>
      <ol>
        <li><strong>太阳光谱</strong>：太阳（约5800 K）的普朗克光谱在紫/紫外区域光子通量较低。</li>
        <li><strong>光谱敏感度</strong>：人眼响应峰值在 507/555 nm；晶状体吸收短波长光（普金耶效应反转）。</li>
      </ol>

      <p><strong>超越瑞利散射</strong></p>
      <p>在紫外波长下，<em>ka</em> → 1，进入<strong>米氏</strong>区（完整米氏级数/球贝塞尔函数）。对于气溶胶（a ~ 0.1–10 μm），米氏散射在可见光范围内几乎与波长无关 → 污染/雾霾天空呈白色/灰色。</p>
      <p>散射光的角分布与偏振态（距太阳90°方向约40%线偏振度）源自偶极辐射图样的矢量本质——与简单偏振滤光片的观察一致。</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

</div>

<script>
// Minimal interactivity: smooth scroll on section header click
document.querySelectorAll('.section-title').forEach(el => {
  el.style.cursor = 'pointer';
  el.addEventListener('click', () => {
    el.closest('.section').scrollIntoView({ behavior: 'smooth', block: 'start' });
  });
});

// Add a subtle fade-in on load
const sections = document.querySelectorAll('.section');
sections.forEach((s, i) => {
  s.style.opacity = '0';
  s.style.transform = 'translateY(12px)';
  s.style.transition = `opacity 0.5s ease ${i * 0.15}s, transform 0.5s ease ${i * 0.15}s`;
  requestAnimationFrame(() => requestAnimationFrame(() => {
    s.style.opacity = '1';
    s.style.transform = 'translateY(0)';
  }));
});
</script>
</body>
</html>
"}

